  $ bond.prisca += 1
* Bring him a lamb
  It is brought in on a cord by a boy from the kitchen, white, a little reproachful, with a pink bow that somebody has tied round its neck for reasons that no one will explain. There is a pause.
  Then the General puts back his head and begins to laugh. It goes on for a considerable time. It takes in Theron, who has put his face in his hand, and the scarred captain, who is making a sound like a kettle, and Meritamun, who has dropped her reed. "Oh," says the General weakly, "I do beg your pardon. It is only that I have been asleep for rather a long time, and I had *hoped* for better of the future."
  He drinks, in the end, with great politeness, and thanks the lamb.
  $ b1.general_meal = "animal"
  $ bond.general += 1
* Say that the Merchant house has hands enough, and let it be hers
  There is a stillness in the room that has a texture, like cold water. Prisca's lips part. She does not say a word. The General looks at you, and then at her, with an expression that would be hard to name. It is not anger. It is a kind of weary, courteous interest, as of a man who watches a friend fall into a well.
  "As you like," he says, quite gently.
  It is done by a steward, in a corner, with the lamp turned down. When it is done, nobody in the room is able to look at Prisca. She sits on her stool with her hands in her lap, and she does not move, and you understand, a little late, what you have done to her.
